    "result_text": "All call sites use the new 3-arg signature and no stale references remain. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key so it's a SHA-256 hash over telephone, email, and the soundex of the last name, and reworked duplicate detection around it.\n\n**New/changed code** (all under `.../rest/function/owner/`):\n\n- **`Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 a standard American Soundex helper (first letter + three consonant digits, vowels reset a run, `h`/`w` ignored, zero-padded/truncated to 4). Deterministic so the create-time check and the mapped response agree.\n- **`IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 now `of(telephone, email, lastName)` returning `Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))`. The postcode is no longer part of the key.\n- **`RejectDuplicateOwner.java`** \u2014 the single duplicate (409) check, keyed on the new identityKey, still skipping soft-deleted owners. The email-domain blocklist step (`rejectDisposableEmail`) still runs before it in `owners.POST.yml`, so ordering is unchanged.\n- **`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 the soft-match now fires when the identityKey **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match (lowest matching id wins). This is what now catches two household members with the same last name and postcode but different telephones \u2014 they get created and flagged `possibleDuplicate`, rather than rejected with 409.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` expression to the 3-arg call, so the response field is now the 64-char hex.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 refreshed the `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `possibleDuplicateOf` descriptions/examples to match.\n\nThe old separate household-duplicate 409 path was already gone from the code (detection was already single-key); I confirmed nothing else rejects on the computed `householdId`. `HouseholdId`/`CountHousehold` remain for `householdSize` and the `householdId` response field, which the spec doesn't touch.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical identity \u2192 409) both pass. BUILD SUCCESS.",
